 # Structural Ghosting with Opacity Modulation
 
-Also called: Contextual Ghosting, Contextual cluster opacity computation
+Also called: Contextual Ghosting, Contextual cluster opacity computation, Structural Ghosting
 
 ## Overview
-Structural Ghosting is a Focus+Context technique that modulates the opacity of non-focus volume clusters based on their structural relationship to the focus region within a classification hierarchy [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visual clutter by rendering context clusters with varying transparency, where opacity decreases as the structural distance from the focus increases [S1, unofficial]. Unlike simple cut-away methods, it preserves the hierarchical context of the data, allowing users to see the surrounding structure while emphasizing the region of interest [S1, unofficial].
+Structural Ghosting is a Focus+Context technique that modulates the opacity of non-focus volume clusters based on their structural relationship to a selected focus region within a classification hierarchy [S1, unofficial]. It solves visual clutter by rendering context clusters with varying transparency, where opacity decreases as the hierarchical distance from the focus increases [S1, unofficial]. Unlike simple cut-away methods, it preserves the surrounding hierarchical context, allowing users to perceive the data structure while emphasizing the region of interest [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-*   A classification hierarchy (tree/graph) of volume clusters.
-*   A set of "focus clusters" $F$ identified by user query or selection.
-*   A "ghosting level" parameter $L$ (integer).
-*   A "color ghosting" flag (boolean).
